      {
        "tipo": "gramatica",
        "min": 14,
        "titulo": "The full article chart",
        "explicacao": "This is the chart that organizes everything. Three shortcuts: (1) FEMININE and PLURAL barely change; they only change in the dative and the genitive. (2) NEUTER matches the nominative in the accusative, and matches the masculine in the dative and genitive. (3) In the accusative, only the masculine changes. Other details: in the genitive, masculine and neuter nouns add -s or -es («des Mannes», «des Kindes»); in the dative plural, the noun adds -n («den Kindern»), unless it already ends in -n or -s. Tip: «dem» and «den» are related to English \"them\"/\"the(m)\" — old English had the same -m dative.",
        "exemplos": [
          {
            "ru": "Der Mann gibt dem Kind einen Apfel.",
            "pt": "The man gives the child an apple."
          },
          {
            "ru": "Die Frau hilft der Nachbarin.",
            "pt": "The woman helps the neighbor."
          },
          {
            "ru": "Das ist das Auto des Lehrers.",
            "pt": "This is the teacher's car."
          }
